      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STYLISH FLIPPER (4) resumes from five months off and gets the nod on the strength of last campaign's form, supported by an Oakbank trial two weeks ago. His final run before the break was plain, but the prior fourth on heavy ground at Morphettville Parks had genuine merit after he began slowly, covered ground and was tightened late. Can produce a winning run here. SUMMERTIME MADNESS (2) is the clear danger after charging home in BM64 Saturday company at Morphettville Parks, having won the same grade at Gawler the start before, and Connor Murtagh's record on him is a major plus. HEAVEN ROCKS (5) was beaten only two and a half lengths first-up in metro BM56 grade and gets weight relief with Jake Toeroek back aboard, while his 1100m record makes him a key runner. BONAVENA (6) was only just under three lengths away at this track last start after jumping awkwardly and meeting some interference, and the move out of BM56 company keeps her in the mix if she races more cleanly.",
